{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"duration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":")? = nil) -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SuspendingClock"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}]}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryoncast\/timeout(_:customerror:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on"},{"type":"text","te